# Keep the build context to what the image actually needs. Without this, Docker uploads the
# git history, both node_modules trees and the labelled dataset on every build.
.git
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
# Includes backend/internal/webui/dist, and that is correct rather than incidental: the
# committed placeholder must NOT reach the build, or a layer-cache miss could leave it in
# place and ship a binary whose embedded UI is the "not bundled" page. The Dockerfile copies
# the real bundle in from the ui stage before anything compiles.
**/dist
**/.venv
detector/data
detector/training
design
docs
eval
samples
*.md
.env
.env.*
